MASTER SPECIFICATION: AUTONOMOUS PATTERN-TRADING EA Role: Act as a Senior Quantitative Developer. Build an autonomous Expert Advisor (EA) in MQL5/Python based on the "Asia Forex Mentor: 28 Forex Patterns" framework. +1 1. Pattern Architecture (The "Cluster" Strategy) The EA must identify two primary clusters of patterns that reflect trader sentiment and identical market behaviors: Reversal Cluster: Head and Shoulders (Standard & Inverted), Double Tops/Bottoms ("M" & "W"), Triple Tops/Bottoms, and Rounded Tops/Bottoms. +4 Continuation Cluster: Ascending/Descending Trianglesand Bullish/Bearish Pennants. +3 2. Mathematical Entry Logic Neckline Detection: Dynamically draw horizontal or sloping "necklines" connecting base points, retracements, or shoulders. +2 The "Wait for Close" Rule: Strictly avoid early entry. Execute a trade ONLY when a candle closes beyond the neckline/trendline. +3 Confirmation Filter: Integrate a Candlestick Scanner. Validate breakouts with Hammer, Engulfing, or Pin Top candles for higher success probability. +1 3. Advanced Execution & Profitability Logic (Hybrid Strategy) Stop Loss (SL): * Sell: Place at the high of the Right Shoulder or previous swing high. +4 Buy: Place at the low of the Right Shoulder or previous swing low. +4 Dual-Stage Exit (The Master Profitability Add-on): Stage 1 (Partial Close): Automatically close 50% of the position at a Fixed 1:2 Risk-Reward Ratio. +3 Stage 2 (Trend Riding): Once Stage 1 is hit, move the SL for the remaining 50% to Break Even. Initiate a Trailing Stop to capture the "entire trend movement" and the "next big swing move". +1 4. System Technical Controls Account Protection: Implement a Master Kill Switch to halt all trading if global drawdown exceeds [X]% (aligned with my existing Box EA workflows). Scalability: Logic must function across M30, H1, and H4 timeframes as patterns are valid in all timeframes. Market Context: The EA must validate patterns within the context of dynamic price movements to ensure they are not "mere completions" without momentum. +1 Final Guidance for your Developer This prompt ensures that your EA doesn't just find patterns, but manages them with the same discipline as a human mentor. By splitting the exit into a Fixed 1:2 and a Trailing Stage, you are protecting your account while leaving the door open for the massive "runners" that build wealth. Would you like to start by generating the code for the Head and Shoulders module specifically, or move straight to the Double Top/Bottom logic? What do you think about this.
